{"title":"Decagon","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>decagon</b> is a polygon with ten sides. A decagon has interior angles of measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a031119d386df3fe72a2f47df29000577a0e46e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, and exterior angles of measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d0d9b28b429ef7a98b6ac8e14b6151af91ed33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. The area of a regular decagon with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f0bda3d13121cb91a2a6bf178bd9894615ad534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{2} a^{2} \\sqrt{5+2\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Decagon&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">Polygon</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">Geometry</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Decagon&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018032513\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 29/10000